<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb domestic vehicle sales rise 11 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb domestic vehicle sales rise 11 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Domestic vehicle sales in Japan in February rose 11.0 percent from a year earlier to 511,375 vehicles, the Japan Automobile Dealers' Association (JADA) said on Monday.</p>
<p>It was the sixth straight month in which sales had risen on a year-on-year basis.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of February sales (with</p>
<p>percentage changes from a year earlier):</p>
<p> Total cars		365,544  up   15.1 percent</p>
<p> - Cars over 2001 cc    85,573  up   17.4 percent</p>
<p> - Cars under 2000 cc  279,971  up   14.4 percent</p>
<p> Trucks		    144,632  up    2.0 percent</p>
<p> - Heavy trucks	   13,079  up   12.1 percent</p>
<p> - Light trucks	  131,553  up    1.1 percent</p>
<p> Buses			 1,199  down 11.0 percent</p>
<p>February sales included 36,759 imported vehicles, up 8.6 percent from the year before.</p>
<p>February vehicle sales by five major Japanese manufacturers were as follows (with percentage changes from a year earlier):</p>
<p> Toyota Motor     201,128  up   11.0 percent</p>
<p> Nissan Motor     111,944  up    5.6 percent</p>
<p> Honda Motor	 50,446  up   33.4 percent</p>
<p> Mitsubishi Motors 42,682  down  2.6 percent</p>
<p> Mazda Motor	 28,981  up   16.7 percent</p>
</text>
